message: "Please cite the relevant theorem paper and computational specification, and cite the underlying arithmetic sources separately."
type: software
title: "Polynomial presentations of the integers over the rationals"
authors:
  - name: "JUVa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
url: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
date-released: 2026-11-08
version: "2026.11.08-v9"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Mathematical papers and exact computational specifications for polynomial
  presentations of the integers over the rationals under stated arithmetic
  hypotheses. The collection proves existence of a 27-variable polynomial of
  degree at most 2^158 and a 317-variable quartic, with ineffective fixed
  coefficient thresholds. Fully specified constructions in 29 variables and
  a quartic in 389 variables are provided separately. Unconditional results
  include degree and coordinate lower bounds, aggregate elliptic trace
  heights, and a single quartic square-root chart over quadratic extensions
  of number fields. Every variable count includes the input.
keywords:
  - Diophantine definitions
  - Hilbert's tenth problem
  - rational points
  - explicit polynomials
  - elliptic heights
  - finite algebraic elimination
  - number fields
